<title>FRANCE: Bank Paribas net attrib profit 1.8 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Bank Paribas net attrib profit 1.8 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable		profit   1,824  vs   loss  2,872</p>
<p>    Total net			 profit   2,647  vs   loss  2,494</p>
<p>    Net bef tax from operations profit   2,878  vs profit  2,322</p>
<p>    Non operating items	   gain	 710  vs   loss  3,481</p>
<p>    Minority interests			   823  vs	     378</p>
<p>    Income tax				     941  vs	   1,335</p>
<p>    Net banking revenue		     13,174  vs	 11,197</p>
<p>    Total revenue from operations,	14,813  vs	  8,935</p>
<p>    Net bef provisions and tax    profit 3,766  vs  loss    470</p>
<p>    Provisions				     178  vs	    689</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank said operating net income before tax amounted to 2,878 million francs and represented a return on equity of 13 percent. Non operating items, which had a negative impact on net income for several years, made a positive contribution in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5071</p>
</text>
